-- title:
--   Places realising primes of an integral model over a valuation subring
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $F$ a field extension of $K$, and $A \subseteq K$ a valuation subring. Let $j \in F$ be transcendental over $K$ and assume $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K(j) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K {j}`. Let $B$ be a subring of $F$ such that the image in $F$ of every element of $A$ lies in $B$ (hypothesis `hconst`), such that $j \in B$, and such that every element of $B$ is integral over the subring of $F$ generated by the image of $A$ together with $j$. Let $\mathfrak{q}$ be a prime ideal of $B$ containing the image of every element of the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $a_0 \in A$ be such that $j - a_0 \in \mathfrak{q}$ (as an element of $B$). The conclusion asserts the existence of a place $w$ of $F$ over $K$ — that is, a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\mathrm{im}(K \to F)$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring — with two properties: first, $\operatorname{ord}_w(j - a_0) > 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_w$ is minus the logarithm of the $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued valuation attached to the height-one prime of the valuation subring of $w$; second, for every $b \in B$ one has $b \in \mathfrak{q}$ if and only if there is an $a$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ with $b - a$ a non-unit of the valuation subring of $w$.
--
--   This is the valuation-theoretic realisation step for an integral affine model of a curve over a valuation subring: each prime of $B$ lying over the maximal ideal of $A$ is the contraction of the maximal ideal of a place of the function field $F$, and membership in that prime is detected by the valuation together with a dictionary of constants from $A$. It is used in the construction of reductions of modular curves and of equivariant torsion reductions attached to a given $j$-invariant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_exists_of_isPrime_over_valuationSubring.lean

